$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for synthesis of aryl thiocyanates 2 A Schlenk tube was
charged with diaryliodonium salts 1 (0.5 mmol) and KSCN (2.0 mmol, 4.0
equiv) dissolved in DCE (5 mL) in an air atmosphere. The mixture was
stirred vigorously at rt for 5 min. Then, the reaction was stirred at
80°C and monitored by thin-layer chromatography (TLC) until 1 was
consumed completely (18-24 h). At this time, the DCE was removed under
reduced pressure and the crude product was purified by flash
chromatography (dry loading with SiO2) using eluents (1:50 ethyl
acetate/petroleum ether to 10:1) to provide product 2 as oil or solid.
Thiocyanatobenzene (2a)[5g] Colorless oil, 56.0 mg, 83% yield. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) 7.44-7.42 (m, 2H), 7.36-7.32 (m, 3H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) 130.1, 129.9, 129.4, 124.3, 110.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on solvent and temperature, alternative
preparation gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Transition-metal-free synthesis of thiocyanato- or nitro-arenes through
diaryliodonium salts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Li, Xiao-Hua; Li, Liang-Gui; Mo, Xue-Ling; Mo, Dong-Liang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2016), 46(11), 963-970

