$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of
3-(6-Aryl-5-phenylsulfanylimidazo[2,1-b][1,3,4]
thiadiazol-2ylmethyl)benzo-[d]isoxazole (2a-f) General Method. Charged
sodium ethoxide (0.33 g, 4.8 mmol) to an oven-dried three-neck RB flask
containing absolute ethanol (5 mL). To this was charged thiophenol (0.53
g, 4.8 mmol) dissolved in ethanol (5 mL), and the mixture was stirred for
2 h at room temperature. Then to this was added bromo compound (1a-f)
(2.0 g, 4.8 mmol) dissolved in ethanol (10 mL) with stirring and refluxed
for 5 h. The excess solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The
separated solidwas collected by filtration and purified by column
chromatography using a mixture of hexane and ethyl acetate (9:1 v/v) as
eluent.
3-(6-Phenyl-5-phenylsulfanylimidazo[2,1-b][1,3,4]thiadiazol-2-ylmethyl)-benzo[d]isoxazole
(2a) 3-[5-(4-Chlorophenylsulfanyl)-6-phenyl-imidazo[2,1-b][1,3,4]
thiadiazol2-yl-methyl)benzo-[d]isoxazole (2b) Brown color solid, Yield:
1.74 g (81.6%). m.p. 213-215°C; IR (KBr) νcm-1: 2934, 2846, 1597, 1621;
1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 4.78 (s, 2H, CH2), 7.74 (d, 2H, Ar-H), 7.86
(d, 2H, Ar-H), 7.10-7.64 (m, 9H, Ar-H), 13C-NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 33.2,
110.7, 121.1, 121.6, 122.4, 122.8, 124.6, 128.5, 129.4, 129.6, 129.7,
129.9, 130.8, 131.8, 133.6, 133.9, 134.6, 135.4, 135.8, 159.4, 170.1,
171.3; MS (m/z): 475.1; Anal. calcd. for C24H15ClN4OS2: C, 60.75; H,
3.16; N, 11.81. Found: C, 60.72; H, 3.18; N, 11.79%.
