$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure A: SNAr of
4-chloro-6-(3-pyridinyl)-3-quinolinecarboxamide 12 with primary
amines/thiols; Synthesis of analogues 13-23 A solution of
4-chloro-6-(pyridin-3-yl)quinoline-3-carboxamide 12 (1 equiv.), a primary
amine or thiol (e.g. 2-ethylbutan-1-amine, 1.3 equiv.) and DIPEA or DMEA
(2 equiv.) in DMF was stirred at 100 °C for 10-16 hours. The reaction
mixture was allowed to cool to RT, then quenched with water, and
extracted with DCM. The aqueous layer was acidified with sat. ammonium
chloride and extracted with DCM. The combined organic layers were dried
over magnesium sulfate and concentrated to afford a residue which was
purified by FC, eluting with 0 to 10% MeOH in DCM. Pure fractions were
evaporated to dryness. The desired compounds.
4-[(2-Ethylbutyl)amino]-6-(3-pyridinyl)-3-quinolinecarboxamide (13)
4-(cyclopentylsulfanyl)-6-(3-pyridinyl)-3-quinolinecarboxamide (15) Pale
yellow solid (105 mg, 81%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d 6, 303 K) 1.45-1.57
(4H, m), 1.67-1.78 (2H, m), 1.82 (2H, dtt, J 3.6, 6.6, 8.9), 3.75-3.86
(1H, m), 7.59 (1H, dd, J 4.8, 8.0), 7.82 (1H, s), 8.09 (1H, s), 8.21 (2H,
d, J 1.5), 8.24 (1H, dt, J 2.1, 7.9), 8.67 (1H, dd, J 1.5, 4.8),
8.75-8.79 (1H, m), 8.84 (1H, s), 9.04 (1H, d, J 2.2, 1H). 13C NMR (126
MHz, DMSO-d 6, 300 K) 24.0, 33.2, 48.7, 123.8, 124.1, 128.9, 129.3,
130.7, 134.8, 134.9, 136.5, 137.0, 139.9, 147.1, 148.1, 148.5, 149.1,
168.3. HRMS (ESI+): Anal cald for C20H19N3OS (M+H)+: 350.1327; Found:
350.1320.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM DMEA can also be used as base
